    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "deadd2ff_6a6fb74f",
        "filename": "kernel/rcu/tree.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 3120,
      "author": {
        "id": 1124848
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-03T14:09:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Strictly speaking, it might be OK. However, KCSAN would have complaints about it.\n\nI said *might* because my recent view of plain accesses on data races have changed due to compiler optimizations.\n\nIn any case, the KCSAN reason should be enough to make it READ_ONCE and it also documents that this is a data-race access.\n\nAnother note, it might be prettier to wrap both the IS_ENABLED() and READ_ONCE() in a different inline function for readability sake.",
      "parentUuid": "aca004c8_da2c5646",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3120,
        "startChar": 69,
        "endLine": 3120,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "f16c8e6e5395b6be4173e9d48317814aa6cc876e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "e594a68c_2d963a32",
        "filename": "kernel/rcu/tree.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 3120,
      "author": {
        "id": 1124848
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-03T14:13:06Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think what Greg is getting at is, there is no data race to begin with because boot time params are parsed before Lazy-RCU can be used. So in that case, it is OK to drop it then. Sorry I wasn\u0027t sure whether you were also planning on doing a runtime toggle. If you are, you could make it a READ_ONCE() in that patch.",
      "parentUuid": "deadd2ff_6a6fb74f",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3120,
        "startChar": 69,
        "endLine": 3120,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "f16c8e6e5395b6be4173e9d48317814aa6cc876e",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "55cbeec2_130f6422",
        "filename": "kernel/rcu/tree.c",
        "patchSetId": 6
      },
      "lineNbr": 3120,
      "author": {
        "id": 1976445
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-08-03T14:23:12Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Another note, it might be prettier to wrap both the IS_ENABLED() and READ_ONCE() in a different inline function for readability sake.\n\nSince this is a backport, I tend to prefer to keep the code similar to the original as much as possible to make potential conflict resolution easier.\n\n\u003e If you are, you could make it a READ_ONCE() in that patch.\n\nIt is a runtime toggle since the permission is 0644. It 0444, but I got an email asking if it can be set to be modified by init scripts. I don\u0027t feel strongly about it and after offline discussion with you it seemed no harm in making it 0644 as the code is correct.",
      "parentUuid": "e594a68c_2d963a32",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 3120,
        "startChar": 69,
        "endLine": 3120,
        "endChar": 78
      },
